729)/64 = 1575/64\\).\n\nSo \\(y = \\frac{15\\sqrt{7}}{8}\\) (positive).\n\nThus \\(C=(\\frac{27}{8}, \\frac{15\\sqrt{7}}{8})\\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 2 – Circle \\(ACD\\).**\n\nPoints \\(A=(0,0)\\), \\(D=(d,0)\\), \\(C\\) as above.\n\nCircle through \\(A\\) and \\(D\\) on x-axis: center lies on perpendicular bisector of \\(AD\\), i.e., \\(x=d/2\\).\n\nLet center \\(O_1=(d/2, k_1)\\).\n\nRadius squared: \\((d/2)^2 + k_1^2\\).\n\nAlso passes through \\(C\\): \\((x_C - d/2)^2 + (y_C - k_1)^2 = (d/2)^2 + k_1^2\\).\n\nSimplify: \\(x_C^2 - d x_C + d^2/4 + y_C^2 - 2 y_C k_1 + k_1^2 = d^2/4 + k_1^2\\).\n\nCancel \\(d^2/4\\) and \\(k_1^2\\):\n\n\\(x_C^2 + y_C^2 - d x_C - 2 y_C k_1 = 0\\).\n\nBut \\(x_C^2+y_C^2=36\\).\n\nSo \\(36 - d x_C - 2 y_C k_1 = 0\\).\n\nThus \\(k_1 = \\frac{36 - d x_C}{2 y_C}\\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 3 – Circle \\(EBC\\).**\n\nPoints \\(E=(e,0)\\), \\(B=(4,0)\\), \\(C\\).\n\nCenter \\(O_2\\) lies on perpendicular bisector of \\(EB\\): midpoint \\(((e+4)/2,0)\\), vertical line \\(x=(e+4)/2\\).\n\nLet \\(O_2=((e+4)/2, k_2)\\).\n\nRadius squared: \\(((e-4)/2)^2 + k_2^2\\).\n\nPasses through \\(C\\): \\((x_C - (e+4)/2)^2 + (y_C - k_2)^2 = ((e-4)/2)^2 + k_2^2\\).\n\nExpand: \\(x_C^2 - (e+4)x_C + (e+4)^2/4 + y_C^2 - 2 y_C k_2 + k_2^2 = (e-4)^2/4 + k_2^2\\).\n\nCancel \\(k_2^2\\).\n\nNote \\((e+4)^2/4 - (e-4)^2/4 = ( (e+4)^2 - (e-4)^2 )/4 = ( (e^2+8e+16)-(e^2-8e+16) )/4 = (16e)/4 = 4e\\).\n\nSo \\(x_C^2+y_C^2 - (e+4)x_C + 4e - 2 y_C k_2 = 0\\).\n\n\\(36 - (e+4)x_C + 4e - 2 y_C k_2 = 0\\).\n\nSo \\(k_2 = \\frac{36 - (e+4)x_C + 4e}{2 y_C}\\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 4 – Intersection \\(F\\).**\n\nThe two circles intersect at \\(C\\) and \\(F\\). The radical axis is line \\(CF\\).\n\nEquation of circle 1: \\(x^2+y^2 - d x - 2 k_1 y = 0\\) (since passes through origin A).\n\nCircle 2: \\(x^2+y^2 - (e+4)x + 4e - 2 k_2 y = 0\\) (passes through B and E? Check: at B=(4,0): 16 - (e+4)*4 +4e = 16 -4e-16+4e=0, yes).\n\nSubtract equations: \\([-d x - 2k_1 y] - [-(e+4)x +4e - 2k_2 y] =